  "conclusion": "corresponds",
  "rationale": "Eval.give delegates to Give; giveShare additionally requires StructReference on the evaluated state and returns a shared reference to the same object. Eval.new evaluates ordered arguments using EvalArgs, checks exact arity, fresh nextId and StructArguments at the final argument state, then allocates zipped fields and returns declaration.kind.mode. StructArguments checks every result when either struct kind is constructed. The displayed guard, mode explanation, intermediate-state equations and failure cases match these premises; state allocation preserves variables and increments nextId.",
